    description: `A link-out listing: the https page your game plays on, on another site (itch.io, your own site, another web portal). Zaisma lists it like any game (cover, gallery, favorites, What's on, the same lists and search) on a full game page marked "Plays on <site>", with Visit instead of Play: players confirm a stop sheet and the site opens in a new tab, never embedded. Browser games only: store pages (Steam, app stores), payment or video pages and downloads are refused. A site other than itch.io, Newgrounds or Game Jolt waits for your standing (get_access). Its site is checked against Cloudflare's malware and phishing list now and every day; a listed site takes the listing down. Free, no cut. To move it to Zaisma's hosting, upload a version and publish it: the listing becomes a hosted game with the same page, link and favorites. null removes the listing. Settings only a hosted game uses (full_game_item_name, demo_game_slug, multiplayer_mode, own_server_urls, account_requirement multiplayer) are refused while it's a listing; minimum_player_age_years 16 or 18 works, and Visit then needs a signed-in player that old.`,
